/* ============================================================
   STUTI — Śrī Varasiddhi Vināyaka Vratam
   The Vināyaka Cavitī vidhānam of the Smārta paddhati of the
   Telugu country, in sixty units, kept in the order of
   performance: the opening verses, ācamana, saṅkalpa, the kalaśa,
   the installation of breath in the image, the sixteen services
   with the three counted offerings of twenty-one, the hundred and
   eight names in full, the dismissal, the stotra that destroys
   distress, the kathā, and the closing Telugu maṅgaḷam.
   Each unit carries its instruction with its English gloss; the
   mantras are Sanskrit, and the closing maṅgaḷam is Telugu verse.
   The Puruṣasūkta stands where the source stands it — by its
   opening and closing words only, unexpanded.
   ============================================================ */
